). The kingdom of Damascus was destroyed by Assyria, but the city revived, and it is as to the latter Jeremiah now prophesies. The fulfilment was probably about five years after the destruction of Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar [JOSEPHUS, Antiquities, 10.9,7]. 

    Hamath is confounded--at the tidings of the overthrow of the neighboring Damascus. 

    on the sea--that is, at the sea; the dwellers there are alarmed. Other manuscripts read, "like the sea." "There is anxiety (restless) as is the sea: they cannot quiet it," that is, it cannot be quieted (

). 

    Hazor--not the city in Palestine, but a district in Arabia-Petraea. "Kingdoms" refer to the several combinations of clans, each under its own sheik. 

